WEBVTT

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:02.067
Your receptionist is mid-conversation

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.500
when another patient calls.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.067
They need a check-up.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.967
Your team is already helping someone.

00:00:07.533 --> 00:00:09.367
After closing, the desk is quiet.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:11.000
The caller still needs an answer.

00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:13.533
FlowAudit builds AI phone agents

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:14.933
around the calls your practice

00:00:14.933 --> 00:00:16.067
agrees they can handle.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.700
One caller gets a clear next step.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.200
The other request is acknowledged

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.533
and kept for your team.

00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:24.367
Here is a recorded new-patient enquiry.

00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:25.900
Hiya.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.333
I just wanted to ring in and book an appointment.

00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:31.100
Thanks.

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:33.200
Can you please tell me if this is for you

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.000
or someone else?

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:35.100
It's for me.

00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:36.300
I'm a new in the area.

00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:38.467
I want to, you know, register with the dentist

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.000
and then get checked up as well.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:43.533
Got it.

00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:44.933
Are you looking for a new patient checkup

00:00:44.933 --> 00:00:45.233
appointment?

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:48.067
The first available appointment this afternoon

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:51.733
is at 2.30 or 3 in the afternoon or 3.30.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.233
Which one works for you?

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.633
Can we do 3 o’clock?

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.133
And the confirmed booking,

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:58.167
shown in a still from the recording.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.567
Your new patient checkup appointment is booked

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:03.667
for Wednesday, the 7th of October

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.267
at 3 in the afternoon.

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.167
These are selected excerpts.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.367
You can watch both full demonstrations below.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.367
Your practice sets the limits:

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:13.567
which appointments, which questions,

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:14.833
and when a person takes over.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.400
Clinical judgement stays with your team.

00:01:17.967 --> 00:01:19.767
We assess your scheduling, forwarding

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.067
and patient-data requirements,

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.733
then agree scope and investment.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.100
Configuration is tested with your team.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:26.767
Activation follows your approval.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.733
Book a fifteen-minute demo

00:01:28.733 --> 00:01:29.733
for your practice.

00:01:29.733 --> 00:01:32.033
Bring the person who can approve the project.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:34.333
We will assess how your team handles calls,

00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:36.767
the setup you need, and the investment.

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:38.933
Then we will agree a useful next step.
